  "facts": [
    "The Roosevelt Island Bridge, a tower drive vertical lift, opened May 18, 1955 as the Welfare Island Bridge, costing $6.5 million and spanning 2,877 feet with a 418‑foot main lift span.",
    "When lowered, the bridge offers ships 100‑foot vertical clearance, yet it opens rarely—most traffic uses the West Channel, with openings mainly in September during UN General Assembly security closures.",
    "Designed to curb island traffic, the bridge feeds directly into the Motorgate Parking Garage, completed in 1974 and expanded in 1990, a key element of Roosevelt Island’s vehicular strategy."
